    "accordion_with_image_CtzmGa": {
      "type": "accordion-with-image",
      "blocks": {
        "accordion_YepL79": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "show_description": false,
            "show_read_more": false,
            "default_open": true,
            "heading": "Why Organic Linen?",
            "text": "<p>Organic linen is an ancient miracle fiber, that contains skin healing and metaphysical properties. It is the only fabric mentioned more than 100 times in the Bible. Linen is breathable, UV-protectant, highly absorbent, moisture-wicking, anti-inflammatory & anti-static. It is temperature regulating, durable & long-lasting!</p><p><strong>LINEN VS. COTTON: </strong>Linen is the strongest and most comfortable natural fiber in the world—highly absorbent, fast-drying, and incredibly durable, lasting up to three times longer than cotton or synthetics. It causes 1.5x less perspiration and is 20% more absorbent than cotton, making it a superior natural fabric. Its production requires twenty times less water and energy than cotton. Flax—the plant from which linen is derived—is the world’s most sustainable and regenerative crop. All of our flax is organically grown, pesticide-free in France, ensuring the purest and most environmentally friendly fiber on the planet.</p><p>Unlike cotton, which traps moisture against the skin, linen effectively absorbs and wicks away sweat and toxins, making it ideal for sensitive skin and conditions such as night sweats, hot flashes, and yeast infections. Its antibacterial qualities may help prevent urinary tract infections, while its natural cooling effect makes it perfect for hot climates. Flax is even used medically in surgical sutures, bandages, and wound dressings due to its biocompatibility and naturally occurring lignans, which have anti-inflammatory properties. Biblically, linen holds divine significance—it was used for priests’ garments, the clothing of saints, and even wrapped around Jesus after His crucifixion. Believed to reduce fevers and soothe skin irritation, linen is regarded as a sacred, healing fabric. Choosing organic linen supports both personal health and environmental well-being: it keeps air and water clean by avoiding toxic manufacturing processes and pesticides, ensuring a purer, more sustainable connection between the earth, the body, and the spirit.</p>",
            "padding_bottom": 0
          }
        },
        "accordion_iwgYpg": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "show_description": false,
            "show_read_more": true,
            "default_open": false,
            "heading": "Organic Linen Advantages",
            "text": "<p><strong>1. Strength and durability</strong></p><p>Linen is considered to be the strongest of all natural fibers. It is highly resistant to wear and tear and strengthens with every wash, making it a long-lasting fabric. Organic linen can last two to three times as long as other natural fabrics.</p><p><strong>2. Breathable and highly absorbent</strong></p><p>Linen is beautifully breathable, and allows more airflow to ventilate your body. It is also highly absorbent, retaining up to 20% of its dry weight in moisture. This makes linen the perfect fabric for hot temperatures, due to it's temperature regulating and moisture-wicking properties. </p><p><strong>3. It's a natural fiber with a lower environmental impact than cotton</strong></p><p>The production process of linen requires significantly less water than that of cotton, giving it a lower water footprint. Almost all of the flax plant can be used, making it a zero waste crop. Plus, being a natural fiber, it is also biodegradable.<br/><br/><strong>4. Naturally insect repelling</strong></p><p>Linen has natural insect-repelling properties due to the presence of lignin, a compound that deters pests like moths. This makes it an excellent choice for long-term storage, as it resists damage from common fabric-eating insects.</p><p><strong>5. Luxurious</strong></p><p>Linen is considered to be the most luxurious fabric in the world, due to its unique blend of softness, strength, and natural sheen, which only improves with time and use. Its rich texture, combined with its cooling properties, makes it a premium choice for essential intimates.</p>",
            "padding_bottom": 0
          }
        },
        "accordion_zcFPF9": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "show_description": false,
            "show_read_more": true,
            "default_open": false,
            "heading": "How is our Linen so Soft?",
            "text": "<p>Heavenly Essentials developed a specialty type of linen fabric, by looping together linen fibers- to create a knitted flax fabric (the same fabric type most commonly used for underwear). This gives all our products the traditional underwear look, feel and softness; except made from 100% organic linen! Our long-lasting linen gets softer with every wash and lasts up to three times as long as other materials.</p>",
            "padding_bottom": 0
          }
        },
        "accordion_mrk4rn": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "show_description": false,
            "show_read_more": false,
            "default_open": false,
            "heading": "Certified Organic Dyes",
            "text": "<p>Heavenly Essentials only uses non-toxic, biodegradable, natural, plant-based dyes that contain <strong>zero heavy metals</strong> or chemicals. Our natural dyes are GOTS (Global Organic Textile Standard) certified organic and NODS certified (Natural Organic Dye Standard). All our dyes are ethically sourced and botanically-based, made from: plants, flowers, fruits, vegetables or minerals. We are exclusively developing herbal-infused intimates, that offer enhance wellness with wear. We strictly use plant-based dyes, and never use colors made from insects. Our dyes do not produce any waste water and are environmentally safe. </p><p><strong>Our white fabrics are exclusively whitened using oxygen and are free from bleach and harmful chemicals.</strong> Heavenly Essentials mission is to create high frequency, healing, heavenly clothing, and therefore do not carry any garments in the color black. Black is the absence of color, and wearing black strains your bodies bio-field and absorbs harmful energy and EMF radiation. All of our colors are produced in small-batches, and dyed by hand at a natural, dye house in Los Angeles.</p>",
            "padding_bottom": 0
          }
        },
        "accordion_jUHzxC": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "show_description": false,
            "show_read_more": true,
            "default_open": false,
            "heading": "Health Benefits of Natural Fibers",
            "text": "<p>Organic Linen is a natural alternative to chemical-laden synthetics, and can help promote skin healing. Linens hypoallergenic and antibacterial properties can soothe sensitive skin and reduce irritation. Synthetic fabrics (like Polyester and Spandex) and toxic dyes, are industry-standard and regularly used for underwear, which are directly absorbed through the skin when worn and enter into the bloodstream- causing a range of diseases and health complications. Microplastics (which includes harmful chemicals like BPA & PUFAS) were found in the blood of people who regularly wore plastic (Polyester) clothing. Heavenly Essentials offers a plant-based, organic alternative!</p>",
            "padding_bottom": 0
          }
        },
        "accordion_iVPkJ3": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "show_description": false,
            "show_read_more": false,
            "default_open": true,
            "heading": "Compostability",
            "text": "<p>Heavenly Essentials underwear, intimates and sleepwear will never biodegrade while wearing or washing. They are actually designed to be stronger and last longer than conventional clothing. Flax is regarded as the most durable natural fiber in the world. <strong>Natural fibers can last up to three times longer, making them a great investment! </strong>Only when your garmets time is up, we recommend planting them in the compost.</p><p><strong>When composted, linen Biodegrades (turns back to Earth) in as fast as two weeks! </strong></p>",
            "padding_bottom": 0
          }
        },
